    {
      "topLeftX": 96,
      "topLeftY": 104,
      "bottomRightX": 225,
      "bottomRightY": 117,
      "content": "# 1. Care of the disc drive",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 128,
      "bottomRightX": 384,
      "bottomRightY": 177,
      "content": "The disc drive requires no special maintenance.\nIt is, however, recommended to clean the objective\nlens from time to time with a piece of wadding, dipped\nin alcohol.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 95,
      "topLeftY": 200,
      "bottomRightX": 265,
      "bottomRightY": 214,
      "content": "# 2. Set-up of the Service Manual",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 224,
      "bottomRightX": 373,
      "bottomRightY": 262,
      "content": "The set is composed of various modules (A through\nZ). The circuit diagrams, PCB layouts and parts lists\nhave also been classified per module.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 110,
      "topLeftY": 272,
      "bottomRightX": 210,
      "bottomRightY": 286,
      "content": "# a) Circuit diagrams",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 297,
      "bottomRightX": 379,
      "bottomRightY": 370,
      "content": "Of each module a functional circuit diagram has been\ngiven, with the incoming signals drawn as much as\npossible at the left-hand side and the outgoing\nsignals at the right-hand side. Each incoming and\noutgoing signal has a unique name, the meaning of\nwhich can be read in the Signal listing.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 370,
      "bottomRightX": 373,
      "bottomRightY": 428,
      "content": "If a signal enters or leaves the module, this takes\nplace via a connector (e.g. 6B2 = pin 6 of connector\nB2) and via a letter indication in the line. This\nindication mentions to which module the line is\nconnected.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 429,
      "bottomRightX": 372,
      "bottomRightY": 477,
      "content": "If the letter indication in the line is the same as the\nmodule on which the signal is present, the signal\nremains on the module mentioned and, naturally, no\nconnector is drawn.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 488,
      "bottomRightX": 373,
      "bottomRightY": 502,
      "content": "# b) Oscillograms and voltages in the circuit diagrams",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 110,
      "topLeftY": 512,
      "bottomRightX": 381,
      "bottomRightY": 560,
      "content": "- The oscillograms in the diagrams have been\nmeasured with a dual-beam scope with Delayed\nTimebase PM3214. The set has been connected to\na monitor by means of a SCART cable",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 123,
      "topLeftY": 560,
      "bottomRightX": 329,
      "bottomRightY": 584,
      "content": "Video : still picture, picture number 5530\n(EBU colour bar, 75% saturation)",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 123,
      "topLeftY": 584,
      "bottomRightX": 378,
