    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 643,
      "bottomRightX": 358,
      "bottomRightY": 681,
      "content": "- The DC voltages have been measured with a\nDigital Multimeter PM2524, still picture, picture\nnumber 5530, unless stated otherwise.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 691,
      "bottomRightX": 189,
      "bottomRightY": 705,
      "content": "# c) PCB layouts",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 107,
      "topLeftY": 715,
      "bottomRightX": 383,
      "bottomRightY": 778,
      "content": "Most modules in the set have been equipped with\ndoublesided copper pattern and plated-through holes.\nFor each module a PCB layout is drawn, consisting of\na drawing of the component side and of the soldering\nside (chip side) with corresponding copper pattern.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 109,
      "topLeftY": 787,
      "bottomRightX": 176,
      "bottomRightY": 801,
      "content": "# d) Parts lists",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 121,
      "topLeftY": 811,
      "bottomRightX": 367,
      "bottomRightY": 860,
      "content": "For each module an electrical parts list is given,\nstating the service code numbers of the specific\nelectrical components that have been applied on\nthe module.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 121,
      "topLeftY": 860,
      "bottomRightX": 373,
      "bottomRightY": 898,
      "content": "The code numbers of the standard components\n(ICs, transistors, diodes, standard resistors, etc.)\nhave been placed on a collective list in Chapter 5.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 107,
      "topLeftY": 908,
      "bottomRightX": 316,
      "bottomRightY": 921,
      "content": "# e) Service code numbers of the modules",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 120,
      "topLeftY": 931,
      "bottomRightX": 367,
      "bottomRightY": 970,
      "content": "In this Service Manual service code numbers for\nthe modules have not been mentioned. Please\nconsult you parts supplier.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 418,
      "topLeftY": 81,
      "bottomRightX": 533,
      "bottomRightY": 95,
      "content": "# 3. Repair on modules",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 432,
      "topLeftY": 105,
      "bottomRightX": 708,
      "bottomRightY": 144,
      "content": "To enable repair/adjustment on modules use can be\nmade of extension PCBs or extension cables. A\nsurvey can be found sub Service Tools in this chapter.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 418,
      "topLeftY": 165,
      "bottomRightX": 521,
      "bottomRightY": 178,
      "content": "# 4. Hidden switches",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 432,
      "topLeftY": 189,
      "bottomRightX": 682,
      "bottomRightY": 214,
      "content": "On Analog I/O module U two switches have been\napplied, hidden for the user.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 432,
      "topLeftY": 214,
      "bottomRightX": 607,
      "bottomRightY": 226,
      "content": "The function of these switches is :",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 447,
      "topLeftY": 236,
      "bottomRightX": 694,
      "bottomRightY": 285,
      "content": "SK1 : +11V or RC5 signal at pin 8 of the Euro\nconnector.\nFactory adjustment is RC5 at pin 8 (switch\npressed out).",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 447,
      "topLeftY": 285,
      "bottomRightX": 697,
      "bottomRightY": 335,
      "content": "SK2 : ENCODED CVBS or NOT ENCODED CVBS\nsignal on CVBS OUT connector BNC3. The\nfactory adjustment is ENCODED (switch\npressed out).",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 446,
      "topLeftY": 345,
      "bottomRightX": 689,
      "bottomRightY": 371,
      "content": "Please consult the circuit diagram of Analog I/O\nmodule U for more details on these switches.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 418,
      "topLeftY": 392,
      "bottomRightX": 521,
      "bottomRightY": 407,
      "content": "# 5. The optical deck",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 431,
      "topLeftY": 417,
      "bottomRightX": 682,
      "bottomRightY": 466,
      "content": "The optical deck in the disc drive is composed of\nvarious critical components and at the production\ndepartment adjusted by complicated alignment\nequipment.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 431,
      "topLeftY": 466,
      "bottomRightX": 700,
      "bottomRightY": 501,
      "content": "For the time being repair of the Deck Electronics and\nof the Laser Detection Unit by a service technician is\nnot allowed.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 431,
      "topLeftY": 501,
      "bottomRightX": 703,
      "bottomRightY": 573,
      "content": "If a failure analysis reveals that the Deck Electronics\nor LDU are defective, the entire deck should be\nsubmitted for repair to the production centre via the\nCentral Repair Procedure of the Concern Service\nCentre. Please inquire at your parts supplier's for this\nprocedure.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 431,
      "topLeftY": 573,
      "bottomRightX": 703,
      "bottomRightY": 609,
      "content": "Repairs on the slide drive assy and the Automatic Tilt\nControl (ATC) assy are possible. See the List of\nmechanical parts for the correct code numbers.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 417,
      "topLeftY": 632,
      "bottomRightX": 515,
      "bottomRightY": 646,
      "content": "# 6. Coding of items",
      "confidenceScores": null,
